From ccbb51bce4082d2874cd3e78097db4b871bb7fe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:29:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] usb: pd: t6050: power up the HPMs, with bounded SPMI
 and HPM commands

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

ported from Omacom m1n1 160b644c, AI-assisted

Replaces our patch 0005 ("usb: skip the USB-PD HPM probe on T6050").
On T6050 usb_init() (called from kboot_boot() before every kernel
handoff) skipped tps6598x_foreach_hpm(), so the sn201202x USB-PD
controllers (hpm0/hpm1/hpm5 on nub-spmi-a0, hpm2 on nub-spmi-a1, all
gen-4 SPMI) were never switched to S0 and their IRQs never masked. A
port used in host mode then has no VBUS. The tree edimoldovan reported
working on J714c (t6050-aurora @ 160b644c, the Omacom m1n1 lineage) does
not skip the probe; it runs it with the bounded transport below, and its
left-rear port is powered.

What is ported (behaviour as in 160b644c; our tree keeps upstream's
GPL-2.0-or-later headers and the i2c enable_power argument):

- usb.c: no T6050 exception, every hpmN with N < USB_IODEV_COUNT is put
  in S0 and IRQ-masked (also "idx >= USB_IODEV_COUNT" so hpm8 cannot
  index past tps6598x_irq_state[]; ccd41355).
- spmi.c: reject a NULL controller, stop draining stale RX words after
  64, widen packed bytes before shifting (89927e5f).
- tps6598x.c: SPMI register selection limited to 1000 polls; each HPM
  command bounded as a whole by TPS6598X_COMMAND_DEADLINE_MS (1500 ms)
  through tps6598x_command_core.c (new file, MIT, as in 160b644c);
  short status/power/mode reads rejected; command failures propagated
  in powerup/enter_kis; init failures free the device; matched =
  HPM_FOREACH_MATCH on the SPMI path; no double tps6598x_shutdown() in
  the debugusb error path (1bbfce33, 3e52d9f1, 6aa43a58, a8848d62;
  Ryan Murray / RyanTheTide, aurora-silicon). Not ported: cold reset,
  usb_cdc, the J700/T8140 paths and the T6050 USB 2.0 host prep
  (65bbd8b6..103ab882), which is PHY setup, not PD.

Added here (not in 160b644c), so a panel photo shows that it ran:
"tps6598x: power state N -> 0 (S0)" when a controller was not in S0,
and "usb: /arm-io/nub-spmi-aX/hpmN: USB-PD controller in S0, IRQs
masked" per controller on T6050.

Worst case with every controller unresponsive: about 6.5 s per HPM
(four HPMs on J716s), instead of a hang.

